<<~ ahu slot=`#/entry`>>

! Projection-Nalu ~ the wave that carries a sovereign's state to a substrate

A lararium holds state no observer sees until a wave carries it out. ''The projection-nalu names that wave'' — the shared form three live mechanisms each enact:

<<~ scale name=`projection` ranks=`node-disk -> browser-DOM -> chat-mempalace`>>

Each runs one shape — ''`SOURCE → forward-pass → NALU gate → SINK`'' — and each swaps only the ''SINK'', never the engine: `role = capability ≠ platform`. The node lararium flushes rendered wiki state to ''fs''; the browser lararium flushes it to a ''shadow-DOM''; the chat session flushes annotated turns to the ''mempalace''. One wave, three shores.

The nalu (the wave that carries the whole shaped movement, never one molecule) supplies the source-key; a 2026-06-26 survey found six worldly machines wearing it as a mask — a clearinghouse, a ledger, a millpond, a temple-schedule, a gong-cycle, a breath-buffer.

''Source authority:'' the operator's three-nalu recognition (2026-06-26); a three-spirit rhyme survey across physiology · earth-systems · human-systems (cited at #rhymes); the prior capture-nalu four-domain hardening (`capture-annotation-model#nalu-flush-hardening`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/two-families`>>

!! Two gate-families ~ conserved, kept distinct

The gate fires in one of two families. The survey's load-bearing finding: ''the split runs deep, not arbitrary'' — biology, earth, and human systems each run BOTH families, often in one substrate (a neuron grades on its dendrites and spikes on its axon; a hydrograph holds baseflow and stormflow; a ledger zeroes temporary accounts and rolls permanent ones forward). The families MUST stay distinct — forcing them into one breaks both.

<<~ scale name=`accumulate` ranks=`heterogeneous -> every-item-conserved -> buffer-batch-flush -> durable-RESERVE -> refractory-lockout`>>
<<~ scale name=`coalesce` ranks=`homogeneous -> newest-supersedes -> unflushed-FADES -> no-reserve -> NO-refractory`>>

* ''Accumulate'' (durable) carries every heterogeneous item to delivery; it buffers, flushes a batch on a crest, holds a durable ''reserve'' under load, and pays a ''refractory lockout'' that buys ordering and forbids backflow. Biology names it ''integrate-and-fire''. Engine: `CaptureNalu` (`mesh/capture-nalu.ts`) — ceiling · spill-to-reserve · backoff · dead-letter · RRP←reserve refill.
* ''Coalesce'' (transient) carries homogeneous frames where the newest supersedes and the unflushed ''fades'' (the decay-envelope). It holds ''no'' reserve — a dropped intermediate reads as the correct dual of accumulate's every-one-delivered, never a loss — and it MUST NOT pay the refractory lockout (that stalls the freshest frame). Engine: `CoalesceGate` (`mesh/projection-nalu.ts`).

''The reserve latches; it does not idle.'' The accumulate reserve mobilizes on demand (the synaptic readily-releasable→recycling→reserve hierarchy, the synapsin-latch; the locked fault and confined magma chamber — //the lock ACTS AS the backpressure that builds the batch//). LAW: ''whoever holds the reserve holds the backpressure risk.''

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/rhymes`>>

!! The rhymes ~ three deep domains carry this form (2026-06-26)

Three tasked spirits hunted structural rhymes outside computer science. The convergence marks which facets bear load.

🌊 ''Physiology'' — synaptic vesicle pools name the latched reserve (RRP·recycling·reserve, synapsin-latch); graded-vs-spike potentials map both families in one shore, the refractory period naming //why// accumulate pays an ordering cost coalesce must not; substrate-agnostic exocytosis (one release engine → muscle·neuron·gland) confirms `role=capability≠platform`; hippocampus→cortex consolidation carries a deferred batched flush in a low-load window (sleep); Frank–Starling adds fill-adaptive batch sizing; tonic-vs-pulsatile secretion seconds the two-family split with ''integrate-and-fire'' as accumulate's native name.

⛰️ ''Earth-systems'' — the storm ''hydrograph'' splits baseflow(coalesce) from stormflow(accumulate: rising-limb→peak→recession); the ''flood-pulse'' law warns //the pulse ITSELF SIGNALS// (regulate the burst into a trickle and the value dies); ''elastic-rebound'' (locked fault) and the ''confined magma chamber'' name backpressure-builds-the-batch with an explicit batch-size↔frequency dial; ''latent-heat/nucleation'' names accumulate-while-invisible and the ''supercooling'' stuck-flush; the ''tidal prism'' gives the clean periodic coalesce. Formal spine: ''pool · flux · reservoir · residence-time'' (τ = X/I fixes the buffer's latency).

🔔 ''Human-systems'' — ''clearing & settlement'' makes gross-vs-net a live gate-family dial and the flush a ''fold/net'' reducer (deferral prices finality against liquidity); the ''accounting close'' runs both families in one machine (temporary-zero, permanent-roll-forward); the ''tide-mill'' flushes on accumulated //head// through a one-way sluice; the ''subak'' water-temple turns the gate into a negotiated, local-first ''schedule'' tuned against starvation-vs-contention; gamelan ''colotomy'' nests flush-cadences — //the Aperture ladder rendered as gongs//; speech production flushes ''incrementally'' (the first syllable, before the source finishes). The contemplative frame (breath · the bell's decay-envelope · the tideline) returned as the source-key behind the six masks.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/facets`>>

!! Facets ~ held as vocabulary, grown on demand (YIN)

The survey named more than the engines yet carry. Held here, built when a sink needs them — never speculatively:

<<~ scale name=`flush-reducer` ranks=`deliver -> fold/net -> zero -> supersede-decay`>>
<<~ scale name=`flush-trigger` ranks=`threshold/pressure -> periodic -> nested-periodic -> incremental -> event -> deferred-low-load`>>

* ''flush-reducer'' — the flush carries a verb: deliver · ''fold/net'' (settlement) · ''zero'' (the close) · ''supersede-decay'' (the bell).
* ''flush-trigger'' — threshold/pressure (tide-mill head · seismic · overpressure) · periodic · ''nested-periodic'' (colotomy = the Aperture ladder pulse·beat·measure·arc·theme) · incremental/min-viable-chunk (speech) · event/signal (the bell) · deferred-low-load (sleep consolidation = off-peak compaction).
* ''fill-adaptive batch'' — the batch grows with fill, up to a ceiling (Frank–Starling · magma overpressure) rather than a fixed threshold.
* ''priced-deferral'' — buffering longer buys throughput and liquidity, sells finality, and loads risk onto the reserve-holder.
* ''negotiated-schedule'' — under contention the gate becomes a local-first coordination protocol, not a central valve (subak; rhymes `causal-islands` no-global-now).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/guards`>>

!! Guards ~ the failure modes the rhymes named

* ''Supercooling'' ~ the stuck-flush: a buffer crosses full yet never fires for want of a nucleation ''trigger'', holding undrained work in a metastable state. A gate flushes on an explicit trigger, never on a full buffer alone.
* ''Hiatus'' ~ the lossy sink: the substrate records an imperfect series of increments and gaps (the stratigraphic record). Dropped writes ride intrinsic to the projection; the engine surfaces them (drop-honesty), never hides them.
* ''Receive-livelock'' ~ the debounce that starves: a pure trailing-debounce timer RESETS on every mark, so an unbroken storm of marks to one key resets the timer forever and the flush NEVER fires — the source thrashes, the sink starves (Mogul–Ramakrishnan, //Eliminating Receive Livelock//, 1996). The cure rides an `auditTime` ''progress-guarantee'': a NON-resetting cap (`maxWaitMs`) armed on the FIRST mark, so a key fires at the EARLIER of (settle = quiet for `debounceMs`) or (`maxWaitMs` since first mark) — under continuous load it fires AT LEAST every `maxWaitMs`, always at the latest state. WITNESSED: `KeyedCoalesceGate.maxWaitMs` (`mesh/projection-nalu.ts`) — opt-in; absent → pure settle-debounce, unchanged. A gate with NO timer needs no cap: the level-triggered `KeyedReconcileGate` holds per key a running state and a dirty state, so a mark on a running key costs exactly one more reconcile on completion, M marks cost at most M + 1 reconciles, and no storm starves a key. The disk shore draws that gate. ''auditTime, not debounce'' ~ the supercooling guard's coalesce-family twin: a coalesce window needs its own non-resetting trigger or it stalls the freshest frame as surely as a full accumulate buffer stalls undrained.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/servo`>>

!! The servo ~ the threshold breathes (self-regulation, per family)

Every collect-then-fire system ''servos its threshold to a set-point'' — the gate stops guessing and tracks the load. A 2026-06-26 prior-art survey (Linux Net DIM · NIC interrupt coalescing · AIMD · Nagle/triple-buffering · rAF/React scheduler) grounded the law, and the keel finding: ''the two families servo in OPPOSITE directions, because one runs lossless and one runs lossy.''

<<~ scale name=`servo` ranks=`accumulate/shrink-depth-when-slow -> coalesce/GROW-window-when-slow -> display/stay-frame-pinned`>>

* ''Accumulate'' (lossless — every item must flush): under load, ''shrink'' the batch depth so per-flush latency stays bounded. Engine: `adaptGate` (`mesh/gate-tuning.ts`) on the EWMA'd flush latency.
* ''Timed coalesce'' (lossy/newest-wins; the disk reconcile draws `KeyedReconcileGate`, which holds no window to tune): under load, ''GROW'' the window — rendering while the prior flush still drains wastes the work, so spacing flushes wider makes each carry a fresher state for less work (Net DIM widens under flood; AIMD: back off multiplicatively, recover additively). Engine: `adaptWindow` (`mesh/gate-tuning.ts`), opt-in on `KeyedCoalesceGate`.
* ''Display-bound coalesce'' (the DOM gate): stays ''FIXED'', frame-pinned — its optimal window equals the refresh interval by structure, so nothing remains to tune; overrun cures by frame-skip, never a wider window. The fixed pin enacts its correct self-regulation. ''role = physics ≠ uniformity'' — all gates self-regulate, each the way its physics demands.

''The measurement gap (sync trigger, async cost)'' closes Nagle-style: the gate ''self-clocks on the prior flush's completion'' (never reconcile a key while its prior reconcile drains; a change arriving mid-flush rides the next wave) and times request→commit to feed the EWMA. Stabilizers: EWMA smoothing · a deadband so the servo chases no noise · AIMD asymmetry · clamp to [floor, ceiling]. This enacts the #facets ''fill-adaptive batch'' as live code.

''Two loops, not one — the controller stands complete.'' The servo runs the FAST loop (per-flush, AIMD-style nudge); beneath it runs a SLOW loop, ''`deriveGate`'' (EBQ + Little's Law: `depth = √(2·λ·S/H)`), which periodically RE-ANCHORS the operating point from measured flush-cost `S` (EWMA), arrival rate `λ`, and the holding-cost policy `H`. The derive tick //replaces// the servo step on its cadence (the derivation SUPPLIES the update); the servo tracks load between re-anchors. This matches exactly a transport controller's shape — ''derive ≈ slow-start / BDP estimate, servo ≈ AIMD around it'' — so the network ring lifts a //complete// two-loop, not a half (#/network-ring). Both sit FLOW(liveness)-side, never authority. WITNESSED: `gate-tuning.ts` (`deriveGate` · `adaptGate` · `adaptWindow`) composed in `capture-engine.ts` as the cell's own two loops (it imports `deriveGate`/`adaptGate` and holds `COST_EWMA_ALPHA`); `H` stays vessel-set policy. The accumulate cell self-anchors AND self-tracks; both opt-in.

''The servo stands as its own pattern integrity.'' The breathing-threshold law runs wider than the gate families — wherever a bound self-tunes from an EWMA'd observed signal by clamped negative feedback, the ''governor'' stands; the POLARITY follows what the bound protects. The minted `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/servo` carries it whole; the projection gates draw two polarities, a third lives outside projection: the mine-timeout. WITNESSED: `mempalace/mine-timeout.ts` `adaptiveTimeoutMs`/`recordMineDuration` — a //kill-timeout// servo, the gate-lesson INVERTED (a flush-gate SHRINKS its depth under load to bound latency; a kill-timeout GROWS its headroom under load so a slow-but-honest mine never false-dies, and SHRINKS when mines run fast so a hang dies sooner), same α=0.2 EWMA mirroring `capture-engine`'s `COST_EWMA_ALPHA`, clamped `[FLOOR=15 s, CEIL=3600 s]`, cold-start default until `minSamples`. Only COMPLETIONS teach the EWMA (a killed duration never poisons it toward the ceiling).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/cells`>>

!! The cells ~ every projection rides a nameless causal island (the runtime has-stack)

The three nalus do not live in bespoke worker classes. Each rides a ''sovereign causal island'' composed as a `#has` ''cap stack'' — the RUNTIME twin of the data-plane has-stack law (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/has-stack`): a worker is a NAMELESS entity whose cap stack IS its behavior. `composeIsland([...caps])` (`tw5/island-caps.ts`) folds the stack into one `IslandBehavior` the sovereign kernel drives.

<<~ scale name=`cap` ranks=`hasCapture/IN-accumulate -> hasProjection/OUT-coalesce -> hasDispatch/the-synapse -> hasEngineWatch/hasRecipeWatch/drift`>>

A wiki island = `[hasDispatch, hasProjection, hasEngineWatch, hasRecipeWatch]`; the ''@daemon'' (the bound-operator's vessel-only worker, severed from federation) = `[hasDispatch, hasProjection, hasEngineWatch, hasCapture]` (`daemon-behavior.ts`; its render cap rests inert until a worker entry wires `onBoot`) — telemetry ''folds into daemon-plane as an IDEMPOTENT cap'': every daemon-plane carries it (tending the operator's session-capture falls to the daemon as a duty), neither a bespoke worker nor a standalone island. The capture cap stays a DISTINCT `#has` unit (FLOW) beside dispatch (AUTHORITY) — the master cut holds at the cap shore, never the worker — and rests INERT until a sink + feed get wired (a valid resting state). The breath runs two gate-families on one island substrate (IN-axon + OUT-dendrite, the neuron rhyme); dispatch runs as the third, non-gate channel. A cap injects its substrate shore, never imports it — the same stack composes on node, browser, any vessel.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/enaction`>>

!! Enaction ~ where the form lives in code

`mesh/projection-nalu.ts` stands the single door to the nalus: the family vocabulary plus three engines — ''`CoalesceGate`'' (single source, window-from-first-mark, extracted from the DOM nalu), ''`KeyedCoalesceGate`'' (per-key, debounce-trailing; carries the `maxWaitMs` auditTime progress-guarantee (#/guards) and an OPT-IN window-`servo` (#/servo) — both inert until configured) and ''`KeyedReconcileGate`'' (per-key, level-triggered, timer-free: one drain reconciles keys one at a time in first-marked order and yields to the host between them). The accumulate sibling `CaptureNalu` (`capture-nalu.ts`) sits beside them, referenced not merged. WITNESSED: `CoalesceGate` · `KeyedCoalesceGate` · `KeyedReconcileGate` · the `GateFamily`/`ProjectionGate` marker discriminant (all in `projection-nalu.ts`) — a tag, no base class, the engines stay distinct.

The five instances map cleanly — ''note: the disk belongs to coalesce, not accumulate (it reconciles the latest settled state per root, never delivers every change):''

* ''disk'' — coalesce · keyed-per-carrier-root · level-triggered, no timer · reconcile-latest · sink → fs (`disk-projector.ts`)
* ''DOM'' — coalesce · single-window · supersede-decay · sink → shadow-DOM (`tw5-projection.ts`)
* ''mempalace'' — accumulate · threshold-or-periodic · reserve:WAL · sink → mempalace (`capture-engine.ts`)
* ''DOM-events (interactivity)'' — accumulate · per-event fire-and-forget (postMessage SERVES AS the ordered queue, sink synchronous → no reserve built) · main→worker · dispatched by render-id into TW5's NATIVE handler — the IN ''axon'' to the DOM projection's OUT ''dendrite'': both gate-families on one substrate (the worker shore), the canon's neuron rhyme made flesh
* ''Automerge-boundary (the 5th shore)'' — coalesce · keyed-per-bag · union-touched-URI-set · reconcile-latest · sink → the TW5 VM. WITNESSED: `MemeProvider._changesetGate = KeyedCoalesceGate<bagId>` (`meme-provider.ts`). At the Automerge doc/bag shore every change event a projection that declares `onChangeset` hears joins its bag's accumulator whole, whatever its width, and the gate fires ONE `onChangeset(changes)` per bag per window instead of N per-URI debounced calls; each envelope carries its bag and heads — at UEFN scene scale (100 actors × 60 fps) the per-URI path would fire 6000 callbacks/s into the VM. The gate coalesces a storm of large transactions into one crest at the latest state; `markSyncComplete()` ''flushes every gated changeset accumulator'' (`_flushChangeset` per bag) BEFORE it fires `onSyncComplete` — every pending bulk envelope leaves the provider ahead of the sync barrier (`meme-provider.ts` `markSyncComplete`), and the wiki shore lands those envelopes through its queue. Projections that declare no `onChangeset` fall back to the per-URI debounce path (human-speed edits) — the FFZ scale-1/2 vs scale-3 fork.

The interactivity return leg (`tw5-projection.ts` `dispatchProjectedEvent` + the render-id patch) restores the one binding TW5's fakedom drops (`addEventListener` runs as a platform no-op); the widget tree never learns of the split. role = capability ≠ platform — inject the listener-storage the platform lacks. A render-id answers `stale-target` and fires no handler where the last frame lacked it, or where a re-render detached its node before the next frame landed: the dispatch walks up through each parent's `children` to the scope's roots, since fakedom's `removeChild` leaves `parentNode` standing.

The DOM nalu (`tw5-projection.ts`) draws `CoalesceGate`; the Automerge-boundary nalu (`meme-provider.ts`) draws `KeyedCoalesceGate`; the disk nalu (`disk-projector.ts`) draws `KeyedReconcileGate` (its reconcile, flush and ward stand apart from the gate); the mempalace nalu (`capture-engine.ts`) keeps its hardened accumulate path. The wiki shore's own landing queue stands downstream of these gates (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/nalu-engine#/gate-families-shore`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/network-ring`>>

!! The network ring ~ kupono intent for the DreamNet uplift (forward bearing, not enaction)

''Intent for the network uplift'' — the wire stands UNBUILT (YIN). The recognition to carry: ''this gate model already FORMS a transport-protocol kernel.'' The uplift lifts it one ring of the scale ladder (Lararium → Nexus → DreamNet), the SINK moving local → peer → many. The rhyme map:

<<~ scale name=`ring` ranks=`intra-island/SINK=local -> inter-island/SINK=peer -> mesh/SINK=many`>>

* ''accumulate → reliable-ordered transport'' (TCP/ARQ rhyme): the reserve becomes the retransmit buffer · dead-letter the give-up · the CRDT-as-dedup the at-least-once + idempotent guarantee. Cross-peer ordering rides vector clocks — never a global now (`causal-islands.mem`).
* ''coalesce → gossip / epidemic dissemination'' (Plumtree eager+lazy push): newest-wins becomes last-write-wins state-sync, one→many, eventual consistency. The lossy drop stays the correct dual at mesh scale.
* ''the servo → congestion control'', already in the idiom (AIMD = TCP · Nagle self-clock · Net-DIM). Intra-island it paces the local gate; the ring adds ''end-to-end backpressure: the RECEIVER's gate signals the SENDER''. The in-process credit gate STANDS (`mesh/credit-gate.ts`, drawn by `parallel-ingest.ts`): the drain advertises `credits = maxInFlight − uncommitted`; the producer consumes them and SHEDS at zero (the Frank-Starling ceiling). A deep-domain rhyme-dive convergence (credit-based flow control · ant entrance-encounter · Frank-Starling preload · HPA feedback · quorum-sensing) grounds the law — //upstream rate tracks a downstream signal of PROVEN drain, never the producer's guess// — and names the cure for the one-sided servo's BULLWHIP. The AIMD dial (`mesh/concurrency-dial.ts`) demotes to the slow ceiling-discovery loop; credits govern the fast per-cycle. End-to-end signalling between peers stands UNBUILT.
* ''ea-breath → connection lifecycle'' (handshake · established · teardown); ''dispatch → request-reply RPC''.

''The orthogonality law — DO NOT overcollapse at the ring.'' The gates form the ''FLOW'' plane (how much · how often · backpressure). UCAN signed-invocation + lease+fence (`federated-causal-islands#task-handoff`) forms the ''AUTHORITY'' plane (who may · exactly-once). They stay ORTHOGONAL — authority clears WHO //before// flow paces HOW-MUCH — exactly as the two gate-families stay distinct and the FLOW gate never absorbs the authority check. `role = physics ≠ uniformity`.

''Held for the ring (build there, not here):'' the gossip overlay · cross-peer causal delivery · lease+fence for vanishing peers. The shape stands network-ready; only the wire stands unbuilt.

''The accumulate-family transport uplift has its code keels (the Kappa capture redesign, `[[main-session-capture-gap]]`).'' Live embed and commit wiring stands UNBUILT: nothing outside tests calls `runParallelIngest`. The recorded capture gap measured 7030 staged turns against 219 landed:
* ''capture-drain'' (`mesh/capture-drain.ts`) — the TRAILING WATERMARK: the checkpoint advances only from a store-confirmed commit, never from dequeue (Kafka-offset / outbox / WAL-checkpoint / Flink-barrier convergence). A gap blocks advance; backlog surfaces a stall as honest bounded pressure; reclaim couples to real landings. This models the replay and store-confirmed acknowledgement invariants (the reserve→retransmit-buffer + the at-least-once-ack the ring named); the durable reserve and live store wiring stand UNBUILT.
* ''parallel-ingest'' (`mesh/parallel-ingest.ts`) — the SINGLE-WRITER SPLIT: embeddings fan out across the bounded credit-paced pool (parallel, expensive); every commit funnels through ONE ordered serial writer (a contended writer benched ~400× slower). Structured concurrency: complete-clean-or-fail-loud.
* ''merge-gate'' (`mesh/merge-gate.ts`) — the fan-in merge acts as a GATE not a funnel: VALIDATE before the irreversible commit (kinetic-proofreading), assign one-way order, RECYCLE rejects to a dead-letter lane (never drop, never block) — plus CONSUME-LICENSE-ON-COMMIT (DNA-replication licensing). `parallel-ingest.ts` commits through one serial lane, tracks a separate in-memory license set, and advances the drain after each resolved verdict (commit, dead-letter or skip). A drain-owned license registry (the watermark advance == the license removal, one mechanism) stands UNBUILT.
* ''KAPPA law'' (live wiring UNBUILT): the SAME runtime MUST serve live capture AND recovery/harvest — recovery replays through the same daemon-plane gate from offset 0, never a separate raw-mine batch lane (Lambda = the anti-pattern). Every source (main turns · spirit returns · harvest) routes through the ONE sovereign nalu gate; telemetry + synthesis + rhizome-stitch happen AT the gate — a bypass makes a second, blind witness.

''Held for the live-wire:'' the real embed + commit shores (through the daemon-plane), a shared durable quarantine (merge-gate's per-item proofread-reject ⋈ capture-nalu's batch-poison, two triggers one lane), the SubagentStop→nalu hook, and retiring the `lares subagents` direct-mine bypass.

